The \fBtop\fR program provides a dynamic, real-time view of a running
system. It displays a header summarizing system load, memory usage, and
per-CPU utilisation, followed by a table of processes sorted by CPU
usage. Both views update on a configurable interval until the user
quits.
.PP
By default \fBtop\fR runs interactively, drawing into the terminal with
full-screen redraws and accepting key commands. Pass \fB\-b\fR (batch
mode) to print plain output suitable for piping or logging, optionally
limited to a fixed number of iterations with \fB\-n\fR.
